Seed the VFIO PCI shadow from the device config space, and return the live
vendor, class, and subsystem dwords to the guest.

NVIDIA vGPU virtual functions keep the physical GPU's PCI ids. Cloud
Hypervisor 51.1 already serves non-BAR config from the VFIO region, but the
shadow starts as vendor 0 and a ConfigPatch can mask the identity registers.
Those bits are read-only, so write_reg cannot seed them. On a fresh device
this reads dwords 0x00, 0x08, and 0x2c (a restored snapshot keeps its saved
shadow). read_config_register returns those three dwords from VFIO and does
not apply ConfigPatch.

Whole-device passthrough is unchanged: the VFIO region already matches the
physical card, so the guest still sees that card's ids. Drafted against
v51.1 without an A2. The guest-visible check waits for the card. A passthrough
of a card that is not a vGPU host is a null test of this patch.

